    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0258" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg184"/>

                <head>Sir F. Bruce to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 25, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The charge d’affaires of Hay ti has
                    requested her Majesty’s government to concur in guaranteeing the neutrality of
                    the peninsula of Samana, a step in which he appears to think the government of
                    the United States might not be disinclined to concur.</p>
                <p>Before replying, her Majesty’s government are anxious to ascertain the views
                    entertained by the government of the United States of the above proposal, and I
                    shall be glad if you can, without inconvenience, enable me to communicate the
                    desired information.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FREDERICK W. A. BRUCE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
